\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. SUNSET and evening star,
\par And one clear call for me!
\par And may there be no moaning of the bar,
\par When I put out to sea,
\par But such a tide as moving seems asleep,
\par Too full for sound and foam,
\par When that which drew from out the boundless deep
\par Turns again home.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Twilight and evening bell,
\par And after that the dark!
\par And may there be no sadness of farewell
\par When I embark;
\par For though from out our bourne of time and place
\par The flood may bear me far,
\par I hope to see my pilot face to face
\par When I have crost the bar.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

